{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall return to HaShem your Elohim.</b> And it is written: ״ושב ה' אלהיך את שבותך ורחמך״ etc. Why all this? As Rabbi Yonatan says in chapter 2 of Yoma: Great is repentance, for it brings the redemption near, as it is said: ״ובא לציון גואל״ — what is the reason? Because of ״ולשבי פשע ביעקב״ etc. — a matter of 'great is repentance,' as is said there. And further, Rabbi Yose bar Rabbi Yehuda said in a baraita: A person who transgresses a sin the first time is forgiven etc.; the fourth time he is not forgiven, as it is said: ״כה אמר ה' על שלשה פשעי ישראל ועל ארבעה לא אשיבנו״. And the reason I heard from Ramal: because there are three partitions before the Holy One, blessed be He. The first: רעש, and after the רעש — אש, and after the אש — רוח, and after the רוח — קול דממה דקה, where the Shekhinah of the Holy One, blessed be He, resides. And in each partition there are angels, and when he sins the first time and comes to the first partition, they restrain him and do not let him pass, and he is forgiven. Likewise the third is forgiven at the third partition. But when a person sins a fourth time and comes before the Holy One, blessed be He, to His partition, he is not forgiven. Thus it says: ״הוי המכעיסים אותי על פני״ — those who provoke Me many times, until their transgression comes before [Me]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "רמ\"ל left as an acronym (possibly a personal name) unresolved; the אש/רוח/רעש quotations allude to 1 Kings 19:11–12."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:38.681296220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}